        <mxCell id="1hEIRoDbOSdjLODKiPfq-42" parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;" value="&lt;div align=&quot;center&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div align=&quot;center&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div align=&quot;center&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div align=&quot;center&quot;&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div align=&quot;center&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;1. Development Methodology&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;2.&amp;nbsp; Testing strategy (make sure people write unit tests, integration tests, HIL, simulation-based regression tests)&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;3. Bring up: CI/CD testing suite&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;4. Documentation practices&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;5. Test scenario coverage&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;6. Key performance indicator baselines (KPI)&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;7. Failure mode documentation&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;8. Agreement/disagreement with predictions&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;9. Assess remaining risks and lessons learned&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
